-- title:
--   The $\mathrm{Poly}(\alpha)$ voting model: stakes $n_{k,t}$, volume $N_t$, shares $\pi_{k,t}$ and voting powers $\theta_{k,t}$
-- statement:
--   There are $K$ bidders with initial stakes $n_{k,0}$, $k\in[K]$, and $N=\sum_{k=1}^K n_{k,0}\ge 1$ initial stakes in total. Fix a real $\alpha\ge 0$. Time is discrete. At time $t$ bidder $k$ owns $n_{k,t}$ stakes, the **volume** is $N_t=\sum_k n_{k,t}$, the **bidder share** is
--   $$\pi_{k,t}=\frac{n_{k,t}}{N_t},$$
--   and the **voting power** (reward rate) is
--   $$\theta_{k,t}=\frac{n_{k,t}}{N_t^{1+\alpha}}=\frac{\pi_{k,t}}{N_t^{\alpha}}.$$
--
--   In each period a single stake is distributed. Given the past $\mathcal F_t$, the stake goes to bidder $k$ with probability $\theta_{k,t}$, and to nobody with the remaining probability $1-N_t^{-\alpha}$:
--   $$\mathbb P(\boldsymbol n_{t+1}=\boldsymbol n_t+e_k\mid\mathcal F_t)=\theta_{k,t},\qquad \mathbb P(\boldsymbol n_{t+1}=\boldsymbol n_t\mid\mathcal F_t)=1-N_t^{-\alpha}.$$
--
--   For $\alpha=0$ a stake is awarded in every period, to bidder $k$ with probability $\pi_{k,t}$: this is the **Pólya urn** with $K$ colours and initial composition $(n_{k,0})$, and every Pólya urn in this mission is this structure at $\alpha=0$.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The chain is encoded by its conditional one-step law with respect to any filtration to which $\boldsymbol n$ is adapted; the natural filtration, which is the paper's $\mathcal F_t$, is one instance. The two step conditions together are the joint law of a period, so at most one bidder is rewarded. Powers are real powers.
-- source:
--   Tang & Yao, Polynomial Voting Rules, arXiv:2206.10105v5, §2, displays (2.1)–(2.6), pp.4–5, and filtration, p.6

import Mathlib

open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory

namespace PolyVoting

/-- **The `Poly(α)` voting model** (Tang & Yao, *Polynomial Voting Rules*, arXiv:2206.10105v5, §2,
displays (2.1)–(2.6), pp.4–5, and the filtration of p.6).

There are `K` bidders `Fin K`, with initial stakes `n₀ k`, and `N = ∑ k, n₀ k` initial stakes in
total. The process `n t ω k` is the number of stakes `n_{k,t}` of bidder `k` at time `t`. In each
period a single stake is distributed: given the past, bidder `k` receives it with probability
`θ_{k,t} = n_{k,t} / N_t ^ (1 + α)`, and nobody receives it with probability `1 - 1 / N_t ^ α`.

The Pólya urn with `K` colours and initial composition `n₀` is the instance `α = 0` (p.5), so a
Pólya urn is a `Model μ K 0 n₀`; there is no second definition.

**Formalization Note.** The chain is encoded by its conditional one-step law
(`step_reward`, `step_idle`) with respect to a filtration `ℱ` to which `n` is adapted. The paper's
`F_t`, generated by the events `S_{k,r}`, `r ≤ t`, is the natural filtration of `n`, which is one
such `ℱ`. The two step fields are the joint law of one period: the probabilities of the `K + 1`
outcomes "bidder `k` is rewarded" and "nobody is rewarded" sum to `1`, so at most one bidder is
rewarded per period, and (2.5) and (2.6) are the marginals. `α` is real with `0 ≤ α` (p.2), the
powers are `Real.rpow`, and `1 ≤ ∑ k, n₀ k` keeps `N_t ^ (-α)` defined; it forces `K ≥ 1`. The
stake vector takes values in `Fin K → ℕ`. -/
structure Model {Ω : Type*} [mΩ : MeasurableSpace Ω] (μ : Measure Ω) [IsProbabilityMeasure μ]
    (K : ℕ) (α : ℝ) (n₀ : Fin K → ℕ) where
  /-- `α ≥ 0` (p.2). -/
  alpha_nonneg : 0 ≤ α
  /-- At least one initial stake, so that `N_t ^ (-α)` is defined. -/
  one_le_total : 1 ≤ ∑ k, n₀ k
  /-- The stake vector: `n t ω k` is `n_{k,t}`. -/
  n : ℕ → Ω → Fin K → ℕ
  /-- The filtration of the rule. -/
  ℱ : Filtration ℕ mΩ
  /-- `n t` is `ℱ t`-measurable. -/
  adapted : ∀ t, Measurable[ℱ t] (n t)
  /-- The stakes start at `n₀`. -/
  init : ∀ ω, n 0 ω = n₀
  /-- (2.3)–(2.5): given `ℱ t`, the reward of period `t` goes to bidder `k` with probability
  `n_{k,t} / N_t ^ (1 + α)`. -/
  step_reward : ∀ t k,
    μ[Set.indicator {ω | n (t + 1) ω = n t ω + Pi.single k 1} (fun _ => (1 : ℝ)) | ℱ t]
      =ᵐ[μ] fun ω => (n t ω k : ℝ) / ((∑ j, n t ω j : ℕ) : ℝ) ^ (1 + α)
  /-- (2.6): given `ℱ t`, nobody is rewarded in period `t` with probability `1 - N_t ^ (-α)`. -/
  step_idle : ∀ t,
    μ[Set.indicator {ω | n (t + 1) ω = n t ω} (fun _ => (1 : ℝ)) | ℱ t]
      =ᵐ[μ] fun ω => 1 - ((∑ j, n t ω j : ℕ) : ℝ) ^ (-α)

namespace Model

variable {Ω : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω] {μ : Measure Ω} [IsProbabilityMeasure μ]
  {K : ℕ} {α : ℝ} {n₀ : Fin K → ℕ}

/-- The volume `N_t = ∑ k, n_{k,t}`, display (2.2), p.5. -/
def total (M : Model μ K α n₀) (t : ℕ) (ω : Ω) : ℕ := ∑ k, M.n t ω k

/-- The bidder share `π_{k,t} = n_{k,t} / N_t`, display (2.2), p.5. -/
noncomputable def share (M : Model μ K α n₀) (k : Fin K) (t : ℕ) (ω : Ω) : ℝ :=
  (M.n t ω k : ℝ) / (M.total t ω : ℝ)

/-- The voting power (reward rate) `θ_{k,t} = n_{k,t} / N_t ^ (1 + α)`, display (2.3), p.5. -/
noncomputable def power (M : Model μ K α n₀) (k : Fin K) (t : ℕ) (ω : Ω) : ℝ :=
  (M.n t ω k : ℝ) / (M.total t ω : ℝ) ^ (1 + α)

end Model

end PolyVoting


